  "geographic_caveat": "MARIDA covers UTM zones [16, 18, 19, 30, 36, 48, 50, 51, 52]. Guinea lies in zone 28. 1 MARIDA scene is within two zones of it, so applying this model to Guinea is a geographic extrapolation: the water optical properties, atmospheric correction residuals and floating-material mix are all unverified there. The model's MARIDA test scores are an upper bound on its Guinean performance, not an estimate of it. Additionally, MARIDA's 'Marine Debris' label is expert visual interpretation of Sentinel-2 imagery at sites with reported debris events -- not physical sampling -- so it supports claims about separability from other floating material, not claims that detected material is plastic."
